1
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,411
[HOST] June 14th, 2015.

2
00:00:26,761 --> 00:00:29,570
In the quiet town of
Springfield, Missouri.

3
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:34,993
On the shared Facebook page of the
best-known mother and daughter in the area —

4
00:00:34,993 --> 00:00:37,946
Dee Dee Blanchard and
her daughter Gypsy Rose,

5
00:00:37,946 --> 00:00:40,836
who everyone believed
was severely disabled —

6
00:00:40,836 --> 00:00:43,469
a short, bitter status suddenly appeared,

7
00:00:43,469 --> 00:00:48,156
announcing that Dee Dee was dead, and
the whole neighborhood fell silent.

8
00:00:50,156 --> 00:00:52,796
[HOST] Neighbors immediately
gathered around the small

9
00:00:52,796 --> 00:00:55,380
pastel-pink house where
the two of them lived.

10
00:00:55,730 --> 00:00:59,163
To understand why a single status
update caused such a shock,

11
00:00:59,163 --> 00:01:01,864
let us hear from a resident
of the same street —

12
00:01:01,864 --> 00:01:06,478
one of the people who watched the life of
this mother and daughter for many years.

13
00:01:07,178 --> 00:01:13,178
[RESIDENT] To all of us, that pink house
was a symbol of sacred motherly love.

14
00:01:14,311 --> 00:01:18,808
Dee Dee was a remarkable
single mother who devoted her

15
00:01:18,808 --> 00:01:22,971
whole life to caring for
her daughter Gypsy Rose —

16
00:01:22,971 --> 00:01:27,634
an unfortunate girl with a
long list of grave illnesses:

17
00:01:27,634 --> 00:01:32,630
paralysis from the waist down,
leukemia, muscular dystrophy,

18
00:01:32,630 --> 00:01:36,794
severe epilepsy, and the
mind of a seven-year-old.

19
00:01:37,344 --> 00:01:43,344
Everyone in this town was moved to tears
by how much she sacrificed for her child.

20
00:01:44,604 --> 00:01:49,051
[HOST] But when police entered
that cold, silent house that night,

21
00:01:49,051 --> 00:01:53,875
they found the mother — Dee Dee
Blanchard — dead in her bedroom.

22
00:01:54,425 --> 00:01:57,545
And Gypsy Rose was gone.

23
00:01:57,895 --> 00:02:00,937
Her wheelchair was still inside the house.

24
00:02:01,487 --> 00:02:04,266
The oxygen tanks and
dozens of life-sustaining

25
00:02:04,266 --> 00:02:06,863
medicine bottles were
still on the shelves.

26
00:02:07,413 --> 00:02:10,1000
All of America was stunned and
asked one desperate question:

27
00:02:10,1000 --> 00:02:13,869
Who had caused the death
of that devoted mother,

28
00:02:13,869 --> 00:02:16,560
and taken away a girl
who, everyone believed,

29
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:19,130
could not take a single
step on her own and

30
00:02:19,130 --> 00:02:21,940
could die at any moment
without her medication?

31
00:02:22,540 --> 00:02:25,812
To get the clearest picture of
the turning point in this case,

32
00:02:25,812 --> 00:02:29,506
we will now hear from the Investigator
who handled this file directly.

33
00:02:31,506 --> 00:02:32,060
[INVESTIGATOR] At first,

34
00:02:32,060 --> 00:02:34,460
we feared Gypsy Rose had been kidnapped

35
00:02:34,460 --> 00:02:36,429
and that her life was in danger.

36
00:02:36,779 --> 00:02:41,179
But just one day later, when officers
found Gypsy Rose in Wisconsin,

37
00:02:41,179 --> 00:02:44,478
hundreds of miles from the
scene... a truth came to

38
00:02:44,478 --> 00:02:47,778
light that stunned doctors
and investigators alike.

39
00:02:48,128 --> 00:02:51,401
When she walked into our
interrogation room that day,

40
00:02:51,401 --> 00:02:53,562
Gypsy Rose was not in a wheelchair.

41
00:02:53,912 --> 00:02:57,590
She walked in on her own two feet.

42
00:02:57,940 --> 00:02:59,495
No leukemia.

43
00:02:59,845 --> 00:03:01,877
No muscular dystrophy.

44
00:03:02,227 --> 00:03:03,829
No brain damage.

45
00:03:04,179 --> 00:03:08,455
And the person behind the plan
that led to the death of that

46
00:03:08,455 --> 00:03:12,731
“saintly” mother... was none
other than her own little girl.

47
00:03:13,431 --> 00:03:17,468
[HOST] Welcome to the criminal
psychology case files.

48
00:03:17,818 --> 00:03:18,235
Today,

49
00:03:18,235 --> 00:03:23,235
we step inside the pink house in
Missouri to decode one of the strangest

50
00:03:23,235 --> 00:03:28,028
and cruelest psychiatric syndromes
ever hidden behind a mask of love:

51
00:03:28,028 --> 00:03:30,042
Munchausen syndrome by proxy.

52
00:03:32,042 --> 00:03:34,899
[HOST] To understand why a
young woman would take such an

53
00:03:34,899 --> 00:03:38,098
extreme step against her own
mother in order to survive,

54
00:03:38,098 --> 00:03:41,469
we first need to look at the
real crime scene of this case.

55
00:03:41,819 --> 00:03:45,151
That scene is not the
bedroom in June 2015.

56
00:03:45,501 --> 00:03:51,501
The real crime scene is Gypsy Rose’s
body, over the 23 years that came before.

57
00:03:53,546 --> 00:03:58,341
[HOST] Gypsy Rose was born in
1991, a completely healthy child.

58
00:03:58,691 --> 00:04:02,963
But when she was just 3 months old, Dee
Dee began taking her to the hospital,

59
00:04:02,963 --> 00:04:05,959
insisting that her daughter
suffered from sleep apnea.

60
00:04:06,309 --> 00:04:09,949
From that point on, Dee Dee
started building an enormous,

61
00:04:09,949 --> 00:04:11,673
fabricated medical history.

62
00:04:12,023 --> 00:04:14,995
When Gypsy was around 7,
after a minor knee injury,

63
00:04:14,995 --> 00:04:18,025
Dee Dee declared that her
daughter had a spinal cord

64
00:04:18,025 --> 00:04:20,997
injury and made the girl
use a wheelchair for good.

65
00:04:21,347 --> 00:04:22,883
She shaved Gypsy’s head,

66
00:04:22,883 --> 00:04:26,274
then told the child and the
whole world that her hair

67
00:04:26,274 --> 00:04:29,602
had fallen out because of
chemotherapy for leukemia.

68
00:04:31,102 --> 00:04:34,582
[HOST] But Dee Dee did not stop at lies.

69
00:04:34,932 --> 00:04:38,794
Going back through thousands of
pages of seized medical records,

70
00:04:38,794 --> 00:04:42,293
police found direct medical
interventions on Gypsy’s body.

71
00:04:42,643 --> 00:04:46,683
Let us hear the Investigator present
the details of this part of the file.

72
00:04:47,383 --> 00:04:49,442
[INVESTIGATOR] To turn the
script in her head into

73
00:04:49,442 --> 00:04:51,442
real symptoms in front of doctors,

74
00:04:51,442 --> 00:04:54,207
Dee Dee directly affected
her daughter’s health

75
00:04:54,207 --> 00:04:57,031
in three ways documented
in her medical records:

76
00:04:57,381 --> 00:04:57,823
First,

77
00:04:57,823 --> 00:05:00,841
she gave Gypsy high doses of anti-seizure

78
00:05:00,841 --> 00:05:04,080
medication even though
she had no epilepsy —

79
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:09,748
drugs that, according to later reports,
contributed to the loss of her teeth.

80
00:05:10,098 --> 00:05:15,068
Second, she persuaded doctors to place
a feeding tube into Gypsy’s stomach.

81
00:05:15,418 --> 00:05:19,215
And third, by describing
false symptoms to doctors,

82
00:05:19,215 --> 00:05:22,194
she convinced the hospital to perform an

83
00:05:22,194 --> 00:05:25,693
unnecessary salivary
gland surgery on the girl.

84
00:05:26,043 --> 00:05:29,783
The big question for our
investigation at the time was:

85
00:05:29,783 --> 00:05:32,706
Why did an entire modern
healthcare system,

86
00:05:32,706 --> 00:05:35,494
with hundreds of doctors, fail to notice?

87
00:05:36,094 --> 00:05:37,966
As we pieced the file together,

88
00:05:37,966 --> 00:05:42,073
we found that Dee Dee had an extremely
sophisticated modus operandi:

89
00:05:42,423 --> 00:05:44,685
She had worked as a nurse’s aide,

90
00:05:44,685 --> 00:05:49,482
so she knew medical terminology and
how to describe textbook symptoms.

91
00:05:49,832 --> 00:05:53,383
In 2005, when Hurricane Katrina
swept through Louisiana,

92
00:05:53,383 --> 00:05:57,885
Dee Dee used the disaster to claim
that all of Gypsy’s original medical

93
00:05:57,885 --> 00:06:02,197
records and her birth certificate
had been washed away by the flood.

94
00:06:02,547 --> 00:06:03,804
From that moment on,

95
00:06:03,804 --> 00:06:06,758
Gypsy’s entire medical
history was written down

96
00:06:06,758 --> 00:06:09,397
by new doctors from Dee Dee’s words alone.

97
00:06:09,747 --> 00:06:15,312
Whenever a doctor began to suspect something
— like Doctor Bernardo Flasterstein,

98
00:06:15,312 --> 00:06:20,601
a neurologist who in 2007 noted a strong
possibility of Munchausen by proxy —

99
00:06:20,601 --> 00:06:23,693
Dee Dee simply stopped
seeing that doctor and

100
00:06:23,693 --> 00:06:26,578
moved on to new doctors and new hospitals.

101
00:06:27,278 --> 00:06:31,679
[HOST] In the pink house built by
charity, the windows were always shut.

102
00:06:32,229 --> 00:06:35,014
Gypsy was not allowed to
go to school because her

103
00:06:35,014 --> 00:06:37,685
mother said she had an
intellectual disability.

104
00:06:38,235 --> 00:06:42,521
Her age was falsely reported as 4
years younger than it really was,

105
00:06:42,521 --> 00:06:47,767
so that she would forever remain a minor
under her mother’s absolute guardianship.

106
00:06:48,317 --> 00:06:54,317
A prison without bars, built
instead from prescriptions,

107
00:06:54,446 --> 00:06:58,057
IV tubes and the glow of charity.

108
00:07:00,057 --> 00:07:05,035
[HOST] At this point, the biggest
question anyone must ask is: Why?

109
00:07:05,635 --> 00:07:08,903
What could a mother possibly
gain by making her healthy

110
00:07:08,903 --> 00:07:12,230
child live like a sick person
for more than two decades?

111
00:07:12,830 --> 00:07:17,397
Many people rushed to conclude that Dee
Dee did it to profit from charity money,

112
00:07:17,397 --> 00:07:21,050
free trips to Disney World or a
house from Habitat for Humanity.

113
00:07:21,400 --> 00:07:26,242
But from the perspective of criminal
psychology and forensic psychiatry,

114
00:07:26,242 --> 00:07:28,259
money was only a side benefit.

115
00:07:28,609 --> 00:07:33,780
The core motive driving Dee Dee
Blanchard’s behavior is widely believed

116
00:07:33,780 --> 00:07:39,025
to lie in a psychological disorder
called Munchausen syndrome by proxy —

117
00:07:39,025 --> 00:07:42,448
known in the modern
psychiatric manual DSM-5-TR

118
00:07:42,448 --> 00:07:46,017
as factitious disorder
imposed on another (FDIA).

119
00:07:48,017 --> 00:07:50,453
[HOST] To understand this
disorder more deeply,

120
00:07:50,453 --> 00:07:53,984
I invited a criminal psychologist
to share their analysis.

121
00:07:54,334 --> 00:07:57,555
Let us listen as the
Psychologist walks us through the

122
00:07:57,555 --> 00:08:00,836
3 psychological layers inside
Dee Dee Blanchard’s mind.

123
00:08:01,536 --> 00:08:06,760
[PSYCHOLOGIST] When we examine the
psychology of someone believed to have FDIA,

124
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:08,638
like Dee Dee Blanchard,

125
00:08:08,638 --> 00:08:14,597
we have to go through 3 layers of
motive, both unconscious and conscious.

126
00:08:14,947 --> 00:08:20,691
The first layer is an addiction to
the glory of the “martyred saint.”

127
00:08:21,041 --> 00:08:22,094
In psychology,

128
00:08:22,094 --> 00:08:25,555
an ordinary fraudster
fakes illness to collect

129
00:08:25,555 --> 00:08:29,242
insurance money and then
disappears to enjoy it —

130
00:08:29,242 --> 00:08:33,229
that is called malingering
(faking illness for gain).

131
00:08:33,579 --> 00:08:37,610
But a person with Munchausen
syndrome is different:

132
00:08:37,610 --> 00:08:43,459
what they hunger for is not money, but
attention, sympathy and admiration.

133
00:08:43,809 --> 00:08:48,576
Before Gypsy, Dee Dee’s life
was a chain of failures:

134
00:08:48,576 --> 00:08:53,793
estranged from her family amid
accusations of petty theft,

135
00:08:53,793 --> 00:08:57,660
a marriage that fell
apart when she was 24.

136
00:08:58,210 --> 00:09:02,273
She was a faint shadow in society.

137
00:09:02,823 --> 00:09:07,513
But the moment she took on the
role of “the brave single mother of

138
00:09:07,513 --> 00:09:12,275
a dying child,” Dee Dee suddenly
became the center of the universe.

139
00:09:12,625 --> 00:09:18,108
Wherever she went, doctors respected
her, neighbors were moved to tears,

140
00:09:18,108 --> 00:09:22,296
and local news stories
portrayed her as a living saint.

141
00:09:22,646 --> 00:09:25,975
Every time Gypsy was rushed
to the emergency room,

142
00:09:25,975 --> 00:09:29,171
it was as if Dee Dee’s
brain received a powerful

143
00:09:29,171 --> 00:09:32,433
shot of dopamine from the
attention of the crowd.

144
00:09:33,933 --> 00:09:37,393
[HOST] But the addiction to
attention was only the surface.

145
00:09:37,743 --> 00:09:41,272
Taking into account allegations
from some of Dee Dee’s own

146
00:09:41,272 --> 00:09:45,166
relatives that she had harmed
members of her family in the past,

147
00:09:45,166 --> 00:09:49,060
the Psychologist goes on to reveal
the second and third layers —

148
00:09:49,060 --> 00:09:51,190
where the cruelty reaches its peak.

149
00:09:51,890 --> 00:09:55,057
[PSYCHOLOGIST] The second
layer is a pathological fear of

150
00:09:55,057 --> 00:09:58,148
abandonment and a need for total control.

151
00:09:58,498 --> 00:09:59,944
When Gypsy was born,

152
00:09:59,944 --> 00:10:03,126
Dee Dee saw in this
child the one possession

153
00:10:03,126 --> 00:10:06,091
that would never be allowed to leave her.

154
00:10:06,441 --> 00:10:09,979
But a healthy child
grows up, goes to school,

155
00:10:09,979 --> 00:10:13,988
makes friends, falls in
love and leaves her mother.

156
00:10:14,338 --> 00:10:19,269
How do you keep a human
being by your side forever?

157
00:10:19,869 --> 00:10:24,561
The dark answer that Dee
Dee’s twisted mind found was:

158
00:10:24,561 --> 00:10:30,561
Make the girl believe she is sick and
completely dependent on her mother.

159
00:10:31,455 --> 00:10:34,996
When Gypsy believed she could not walk on

160
00:10:34,996 --> 00:10:38,709
her own and could not
take care of herself,

161
00:10:38,709 --> 00:10:44,668
Dee Dee became the only one holding
her daughter’s life in her hands.

162
00:10:46,668 --> 00:10:49,298
[PSYCHOLOGIST] And
finally, the third layer:

163
00:10:49,298 --> 00:10:53,922
the psychological signature
of erasing an identity.

164
00:10:54,272 --> 00:10:57,292
We paid special attention
to the fact that Dee

165
00:10:57,292 --> 00:11:00,050
Dee regularly shaved Gypsy’s head and made

166
00:11:00,050 --> 00:11:03,004
her wear brightly colored
children’s princess

167
00:11:03,004 --> 00:11:05,893
dresses even when she
was over 20 years old.

168
00:11:06,243 --> 00:11:09,564
It was not only about faking cancer.

169
00:11:09,914 --> 00:11:15,149
It was infantilization — the
stripping away of adulthood.

170
00:11:15,499 --> 00:11:20,747
She would not allow Gypsy’s
body to grow into a woman’s.

171
00:11:21,297 --> 00:11:24,119
In Dee Dee’s imagined script,

172
00:11:24,119 --> 00:11:30,119
Gypsy had to remain forever a
fragile 7-year-old porcelain doll,

173
00:11:30,346 --> 00:11:34,044
held entirely in the palm of her hand.

174
00:11:36,044 --> 00:11:40,015
[HOST] When the case came to light,
alongside the outrage at the mother,

175
00:11:40,015 --> 00:11:44,659
many people also began asking a skeptical
question about Gypsy Rose herself.

176
00:11:45,009 --> 00:11:48,968
Let us hear a very typical question
from a viewer who followed the case.

177
00:11:49,668 --> 00:11:52,797
[VIEWER] There is one thing
I just cannot understand:

178
00:11:52,797 --> 00:11:56,851
She knew perfectly well that
her legs were not paralyzed.

179
00:11:57,201 --> 00:12:02,229
Every night, alone in her room, she would
still get up and walk around normally.

180
00:12:02,579 --> 00:12:04,496
So why, in all those years,

181
00:12:04,496 --> 00:12:08,755
in front of hundreds of doctors,
police officers and crowds,

182
00:12:08,755 --> 00:12:13,938
did Gypsy never once stand up from
that wheelchair and expose her mother?

183
00:12:15,938 --> 00:12:17,422
[HOST] To answer this question,

184
00:12:17,422 --> 00:12:20,142
we cannot apply the
thinking of a free adult

185
00:12:20,142 --> 00:12:22,800
to a child who grew up
inside a glass cage.

186
00:12:23,150 --> 00:12:26,417
Let us return to the
Psychologist to decode Gypsy’s

187
00:12:26,417 --> 00:12:29,876
silence through two powerful
psychological mechanisms:

188
00:12:29,876 --> 00:12:32,438
learned helplessness and trauma bonding.

189
00:12:33,138 --> 00:12:37,774
[PSYCHOLOGIST] The concept of learned
helplessness was first described by

190
00:12:37,774 --> 00:12:42,251
psychologist Martin Seligman
and his colleagues in 1967.

191
00:12:42,601 --> 00:12:47,704
When an animal is exposed again and
again to stress it cannot escape,

192
00:12:47,704 --> 00:12:50,588
and every attempt to resist is useless,

193
00:12:50,588 --> 00:12:55,617
the brain reaches a fixed conclusion:
“All struggle is meaningless.”

194
00:12:55,967 --> 00:13:01,705
From that moment on, even when
the cage door is wide open,

195
00:13:01,705 --> 00:13:07,705
the animal will lie still and
endure, and never walk out again.

196
00:13:08,488 --> 00:13:11,104
Now look at the world
through Gypsy’s eyes,

197
00:13:11,104 --> 00:13:14,084
from the moment she was
old enough to understand:

198
00:13:14,434 --> 00:13:20,434
Every time they sat in front of a doctor,
Dee Dee would hold Gypsy’s hand tightly.

199
00:13:20,845 --> 00:13:24,746
To outsiders, it was the
tender gesture of a mother.

200
00:13:25,096 --> 00:13:31,096
But to Gypsy, it was a secret threat:
If she said even one wrong word,

201
00:13:32,035 --> 00:13:38,035
or showed that she was healthy, that
grip would tighten like a silent warning.

202
00:13:40,317 --> 00:13:45,445
And when the door of the pink
house closed after the appointment,

203
00:13:45,445 --> 00:13:50,651
harsh punishment and suffocating
control would be waiting for her.

204
00:13:52,151 --> 00:13:54,972
[HOST] In fact, Gypsy
did try to save herself.

205
00:13:55,322 --> 00:13:59,504
In the case file, the Investigator
found an incident from 2011 —

206
00:13:59,504 --> 00:14:04,666
an incident that completely extinguished
this young woman’s last spark of hope.

207
00:14:05,216 --> 00:14:07,909
Let us hear the details
from the Investigator.

208
00:14:08,609 --> 00:14:11,292
[INVESTIGATOR] According to
accounts from Gypsy and others,

209
00:14:11,292 --> 00:14:13,182
in 2011, when she was about 19,

210
00:14:13,182 --> 00:14:18,303
she secretly left home to be with a man she
had met at a science fiction convention,

211
00:14:18,303 --> 00:14:20,254
hoping he would help her escape.

212
00:14:20,604 --> 00:14:24,758
But Dee Dee soon tracked
her down at a hotel.

213
00:14:25,108 --> 00:14:29,555
There, in front of the man, Dee Dee
produced paperwork with a false,

214
00:14:29,555 --> 00:14:33,217
younger birth date that made
Gypsy appear to be a minor,

215
00:14:33,217 --> 00:14:35,441
and threatened to call the police.

216
00:14:35,791 --> 00:14:39,265
Once again, people believed
the “saintly” mother,

217
00:14:39,265 --> 00:14:42,455
and Gypsy was brought
back to the pink house.

218
00:14:43,005 --> 00:14:45,268
Afterward, by Gypsy’s account,

219
00:14:45,268 --> 00:14:48,586
Dee Dee destroyed her
phone and computer and

220
00:14:48,586 --> 00:14:52,131
warned her never to step
out of the door again.

221
00:14:54,131 --> 00:14:58,072
[HOST] That shock in 2011 sealed
one belief in Gypsy’s mind:

222
00:14:58,072 --> 00:15:02,905
The outside world would never
believe a girl labeled as disabled;

223
00:15:02,905 --> 00:15:06,102
it would only believe
her wonderful mother.

224
00:15:06,652 --> 00:15:07,598
And beyond fear,

225
00:15:07,598 --> 00:15:11,679
the Psychologist points to another
invisible thread binding the girl.

226
00:15:12,379 --> 00:15:15,964
[PSYCHOLOGIST] It is
called trauma bonding.

227
00:15:16,314 --> 00:15:20,030
Dee Dee was the one
causing Gypsy’s illnesses,

228
00:15:20,030 --> 00:15:25,037
yet Dee Dee was also the only
person who held her every night,

229
00:15:25,037 --> 00:15:29,480
brushed her hair and called
her “Mommy’s little angel.”

230
00:15:30,030 --> 00:15:33,830
The mix of harsh control
and smothering indulgence

231
00:15:33,830 --> 00:15:37,630
paralyzed Gypsy’s ability
to recognize boundaries.

232
00:15:38,330 --> 00:15:41,476
[HOST] When every legal
way out seemed sealed off,

233
00:15:41,476 --> 00:15:47,037
a mind that had been held down for 23
years turned to the most extreme exit.

234
00:15:47,587 --> 00:15:50,237
Online, Gypsy met Nicholas Godejohn —

235
00:15:50,237 --> 00:15:53,531
a young man from Wisconsin
whose lawyers later

236
00:15:53,531 --> 00:15:57,183
argued at trial that he
was on the autism spectrum.

237
00:15:57,733 --> 00:16:01,442
Some observers have compared
what developed between

238
00:16:01,442 --> 00:16:05,006
these two isolated young
people to folie à deux —

239
00:16:05,006 --> 00:16:06,752
a madness shared by two.

240
00:16:07,302 --> 00:16:10,104
Gypsy has said she came to
believe that only if her

241
00:16:10,104 --> 00:16:12,852
mother were gone could she
live a life of her own.

242
00:16:13,402 --> 00:16:15,707
And on a night in June 2015,

243
00:16:15,707 --> 00:16:19,493
the tragedy erupted when
Gypsy opened the door

244
00:16:19,493 --> 00:16:23,033
for Godejohn to walk
into the pink house...

245
00:16:25,033 --> 00:16:26,526
[HOST] In a Missouri courtroom,

246
00:16:26,526 --> 00:16:31,314
the case of Gypsy Rose Blanchard sparked
an intense legal and ethical debate.

247
00:16:31,664 --> 00:16:32,190
Legally,

248
00:16:32,190 --> 00:16:35,279
helping to plan an act
that led to the death of

249
00:16:35,279 --> 00:16:38,434
one’s own mother is
undeniably a serious felony.

250
00:16:38,784 --> 00:16:42,192
But Greene County prosecuting
attorney Dan Patterson said that,

251
00:16:42,192 --> 00:16:46,087
although he believed he could have
won a first-degree murder conviction,

252
00:16:46,087 --> 00:16:47,602
it would not have been fair,

253
00:16:47,602 --> 00:16:51,172
given the years of abuse Gypsy had
suffered at her mother’s hands.

254
00:16:52,672 --> 00:16:54,894
[HOST] In 2016, under a plea agreement,

255
00:16:54,894 --> 00:16:57,811
Gypsy Rose pleaded guilty to second-degree

256
00:16:57,811 --> 00:17:01,145
murder and was sentenced
to 10 years in prison —

257
00:17:01,145 --> 00:17:03,923
the minimum for that charge in Missouri.

258
00:17:04,273 --> 00:17:08,364
Perhaps the most heartbreaking
words came from Gypsy herself,

259
00:17:08,364 --> 00:17:10,779
in a TV interview after her release:

260
00:17:10,779 --> 00:17:15,273
“I also had more freedom in prison
than I ever had with my mother.”

261
00:17:15,823 --> 00:17:18,084
At the end of December 2023,

262
00:17:18,084 --> 00:17:23,091
after serving 85% of her sentence,
she was released on parole.

263
00:17:25,091 --> 00:17:27,278
[HOST] Looking back at
the entire case file,

264
00:17:27,278 --> 00:17:30,646
so that similar tragedies can
no longer hide in the dark,

265
00:17:30,646 --> 00:17:34,724
we will hear the Psychologist and
the Investigator sum up 4 red flags

266
00:17:34,724 --> 00:17:38,802
that help the community recognize
Munchausen syndrome by proxy early.

267
00:17:39,502 --> 00:17:43,922
[PSYCHOLOGIST] The first sign: A
child or dependent person has a dense,

268
00:17:43,922 --> 00:17:46,921
unusual, never-ending medical history,

269
00:17:46,921 --> 00:17:52,841
while objective test results always
contradict the caregiver’s description.

270
00:17:53,191 --> 00:17:57,919
The second sign: Symptoms appear
only when the caregiver is present,

271
00:17:57,919 --> 00:18:00,839
and clearly improve as soon as the patient

272
00:18:00,839 --> 00:18:03,759
is separated or under camera surveillance.

273
00:18:04,459 --> 00:18:05,365
[INVESTIGATOR] The third sign:

274
00:18:05,365 --> 00:18:09,413
The caregiver seems overly eager
about invasive medical procedures,

275
00:18:09,413 --> 00:18:13,339
likes to show off the child’s
illness on social media for praise,

276
00:18:13,339 --> 00:18:17,870
and immediately changes doctors whenever
someone asks a skeptical question.

277
00:18:18,220 --> 00:18:21,820
And the fourth sign: The
victim is isolated from school,

278
00:18:21,820 --> 00:18:26,448
friends and other relatives on the
pretext of “protecting their health.”

279
00:18:28,948 --> 00:18:32,557
[HOST] The file on the pink
house in Missouri is now closed,

280
00:18:32,557 --> 00:18:38,073
but its echo remains a sharp reminder of
the many-sided nature of the human mind.

281
00:18:38,623 --> 00:18:41,830
True love always aims to
help a child grow up healthy,

282
00:18:41,830 --> 00:18:44,858
independent and able to
walk on their own two feet.

283
00:18:45,208 --> 00:18:47,696
When love is twisted into a cage,

284
00:18:47,696 --> 00:18:53,048
when care becomes a tool to satisfy
an adult’s selfish ego... then what

285
00:18:53,048 --> 00:18:58,475
wears the robe of an angel can sometimes
be as devastating as any crime.

286
00:18:59,975 --> 00:19:03,295
[HOST] Thank you to our guests for
analyzing this case file with us,

287
00:19:03,295 --> 00:19:06,616
and thank you for listening to
the very end of today’s story.

288
00:19:06,966 --> 00:19:09,270
Leave your perspective in the comments,

289
00:19:09,270 --> 00:19:12,284
keep a clear head, and see
you in the next episode.
